    {
      "slug": "whipping-thread",
      "term": "Whipping thread",
      "definition": "The second thread that spirals over the foundation stitches without entering the fabric. A blunt tapestry needle prevents splitting the foundation thread."
    }
  ],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Whipped back stitch uses a ",
            "type": "text"
          },
          {
            "text": "whipping thread",
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "whipping-thread"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": " carried on a blunt tapestry needle to spiral over the back stitch foundation. The whipping never enters the fabric; it slides under each stitch in one direction only to create a consistent twisted cord.",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "What you need",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "suppliesCard",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Foundation thread",
              "value": "Stranded cotton, 2 strands in colour A"
            },
            {
              "label": "Whipping thread",
              "value": "Stranded cotton, 2 strands in colour B; or perle 12 for a rounder cord"
            },
            {
              "label": "Fabric",
              "value": "Linen or cotton muslin"
            },
            {
              "label": "Needles",
              "value": "Embroidery needle size 9 for foundation; tapestry needle size 24 for whipping"
            },
            {
              "label": "Hoop",
              "value": "15 cm embroidery hoop"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Working a practice piece",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Work a line of back stitch along the transfer line with colour A.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Thread the tapestry needle with colour B. Bring it up at the start of the back stitch line, under the first stitch.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Slide the blunt needle under each back stitch in turn, from the same side each time. Do not enter the fabric.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "text": "Continue to the end of the line and fasten off under the last few whipping loops at the back.",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Common mistakes",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "intro": "Two common problems.",
          "items": [
            {
              "fix": "Always use a blunt tapestry needle for the whipping pass. The blunt tip slides under the foundation rather than piercing it.",
              "cause": "Using a sharp needle for whipping.",
              "symptom": "The whipping thread splits the foundation stitches"
            },
            {
              "fix": "Pick a direction and stay with it for the whole line.",
              "cause": "The whipping needle is going under stitches from alternating sides.",
              "symptom": "The cord looks loose on one side"
            }
          ],
          "heading": "When whipped back stitch goes wrong"
        }
      },
